---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/code-block.astro';
import GuidePage from '../../layouts/guide-page.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Getting started"
  lead="Nib is CSS first: one stylesheet styles every component. Add a binding only for the interactive ones."
>
  <h2 id="packages">The packages</h2>
  <div class="nib-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Packages" tabindex="0">
    <table class="nib-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Package</th>
          <th scope="col">What it holds</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>@nib-ui/css</code>
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>nib.css</code> (tokens, base and every component), single components, <code>utilities.css</code> and
            the presets
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>@nib-ui/tokens</code>
          </td>
          <td>The design tokens as CSS variables, a Tailwind v4 theme and JSON</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>@nib-ui/fonts</code>
          </td>
          <td>Inter and JetBrains Mono, self-hosted; optional</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>@nib-ui/icons</code>
          </td>
          <td>The icon set as CSS masks, a sprite and ES modules</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>@nib-ui/js</code>
          </td>
          <td>Interactive components wired from markup, no framework</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>@nib-ui/react</code>, <code>vue</code>, <code>svelte</code>
          </td>
          <td>The same components as hooks, composables and stores</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>@nib-ui/core</code>, <code>@nib-ui/dom</code>
          </td>
          <td>The headless controllers and their DOM adapters, used by every binding</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>@nib-ui/cli</code>
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>nib init</code>, <code>nib theme check</code> and <code>nib lint</code>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="quick">The quickest start</h2>
  <p>The CLI asks for a preset and how you load CSS, then writes the files a project needs.</p>
  <CodeBlock
    label="shell"
    code={`npx @nib-ui/cli init
pnpm add @nib-ui/css @nib-ui/tokens @nib-ui/fonts`}
  />
  <p>
    Then import the CSS entry it wrote once, before your own styles. Continue with <a href="/guides/css/">plain CSS</a>
    or <a href="/guides/tailwind/">Tailwind</a>, and for interactive components with
    <a href="/guides/javascript/">vanilla JS</a>, <a href="/guides/react/">React</a>,<a href="/guides/vue/">Vue</a> or{' '}
    <a href="/guides/svelte/">Svelte</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="browsers">Browsers</h2>
  <p>
    The last two versions of Chrome, Firefox and Safari. Nib uses a feature only when all three have it, with no
    fallbacks; each minor release records its browserslist snapshot in the changelog.
  </p>
</GuidePage>
